  "sections": {
    "BASICS": {
      "present": true,
      "status": "content",
      "content_blocks": [],
      "subsections": {
        "OVERVIEW": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "canonical_heading": "OVERVIEW",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Five types—trichoepithelioma and trichoblastoma are most common types, but uncommon types include infundibular keratinizing acanthoma, tricholemmoma, and pilomatricoma; these are differentiated based on their origin: trichoepithelioma, trichoblastoma, infundibular keratinizing acanthoma, and tricholemmoma, which arise from keratinocytes in the outer root sheath of the hair follicle (± hair matrix); and pilomatri-",
              "pdf_page": 660,
              "printed_page": 578,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "coma, which arises from the hair matrix.",
              "pdf_page": 660,
              "printed_page": 578,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "All types—generally benign; a few published reports of malignant trichoepitheliomas, trichoblastomas, and pilomatricomas.",
              "pdf_page": 660,
              "printed_page": 578,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Approximately 5% of all skin tumors in dogs and 1% of all skin tumors in cats.",
              "pdf_page": 660,
              "printed_page": 578,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
